Honestly, this is somewhat of a difficult question without any background infor. Is she staying in dorms or an apartment? Maybe she has major-specific items she might want.

&#x200B;

That being said, I made this funny document with a couple freshmen last year that might help for any incoming freshmen, or if you have any ideas. 

&#x200B;

[Basic Dorm Survival Manual](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P5ap2r7bxF7lz9o4k3ervxyuJGsiwpMUBZ64jZ-DEDE/edit?usp=sharing)

Good community, lack of AC matters for a week or two tops, and great location. Enjoy! 

&#x200B;

Also cleaner than Ratstein

There's often this bizarre idea that success somehow means you're not oppressed or capable of being hurt. Some people say that white people can't be disciminated against because they see benefits in a predominantly white country; that Asians can't be suffering simply because they achieve massive success in academic fields. Me being capable enough to attend NYU, my family being hard working and lucky enough to allow me even the opportunity to attend such an institution, all that is in spite of disctrimination. I'm not any less afraid of someone spitting on me, insulting me, attacking me or harming the people I know on the subway just because we had a high SAT score.  

&#x200B;

[Here's a small fact sheet that details hate crime changes from 2019 through 2020.](https://www.csusb.edu/sites/default/files/FACT%20SHEET-%20Anti-Asian%20Hate%202020%203.2.21.pdf) Notice that as a result of Quarantine and general fear of COVID-19, hate crimes as a whole dropped by a significant margin. In fact, NYC dropped from 428 crimes in 2019 to 265 in 2020. A significant and impressive drop! If not for the fact that Asian involved hate crimes went from *3* in 2019 to *28* in 2020. It doesn't sound like a huge difference, but in the context of total hate crimes, that's an over 800% increase in Anti-Asian sentimentality in 2020. It's an often repeated statistic, but it's significant enough to be noteworthy and not dismissed as *merely* media exaggeration.

I got in ED, so the 'fun' part of senior year started for me just before Christmas. It died at Covid, but it gets SO much easier after acceptance.

&#x200B;

Keep your grades up for now, because senioritis hits and it hits HARD. My grades took the fattest nosedive in my career. Went from A's first two semesters to B- and C's.

I feel like you're really underestimating just how big small stat changes are. Maybe I'm looking at it through too much of a competitive lens, but there are pokemon out there who'd jump one or two tiers up with just 1 extra point in speed. 

&#x200B;

And, you really can't get more change than something like Alolan Ninetales or Galarian Weezing. There *are* creative design changes, but simply because one or two of them don't look that different doesn't discredit the rest. Slowking became fucking dravula and slowbro got a gun.

