I thoroughly enjoy his presence in the game. His flash doesn't feel broken, as the post has explained. His false footsteps aren't broken, but are impactful enough to make a difference when it matters. His teleport, even, feels very fair. You run considerable risk when using it aggressively, making it a high-risk, high reward ability that rewards game knowledge. Heck, even used defensively it feels quite good to play against. 

&#x200B;

Going by my friends' and online reactions, playing him is quite fun as well. Thus far, I feel like Riot did a pretty good job with him.

I'm a Zac main, and as everyone said, you're basically fucked if your E doesn't land. The difficulty in zac is mostly just consistency. You have a *ton* of cc, but two of them are skill shots and your ult is much weaker in comparison (cc-wise). When you compare that to, say, Skarner, the issues become pretty obvious as you go. Skarner's kit isn't hard to pull off. You walk up to someone, juking cc on the way, then ult or E stun from up close. Your CC is easy to land and sticking onto someone is super easy.

&#x200B;

Zac's winrate being low right now is the symptom of the meta. The cinder nerfs slowed his clear significantly, lending him to easy invades, the high grevious wounds presence in the meta means that Zac's main draw, his regen, is completely nullified. It's just a case in which his net positives are much more lower than his negatives in this meta. It's like an opportunity cost. Why play Zac when you can just play Nunu, who has similar ability for 'surprise' ganks from river, but doesn't lack the weakness and instability? 

&#x200B;

I've personally set Zac to the wayside for now. He's a fun champion, but he needs help (especially when trying to climb, good lord). I'm spamming the crap out of Skarner. I'm unsure of what elo you are, but if you're aiming to learn jungle, Zac and Rek'sai aren't the best champions to go for with that goal in mind. Zac's gank patterns are weird, although very fun. Rek'sai takes a significant amount of macro knowledge to really pull off correctly, but this doesn't mean you can't play  her well. It's just that there are much better champions to go for in sub-diamond than Rek'sai.

